    {
      "id": "wg9y3p5",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "2.1.1 Location and Extent"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "pcl5ny5",
      "content": "Gujarat is located in the western part of India. It lies between 20°1' to 24°7' North latitude and 68°4' to 74°4' East longitude. Gujarat has the longest coastline of any Indian state — approximately 1,600 km (some estimates say 1,665 km)."
    },
    {
      "id": "95f3jbx",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "Area: 1,96,024 sq. km (6th largest state in India by area)",
        "Population: Approx. 6.27 crore (2011 Census) — about 5.2% of India's population",
        "Capital: Gandhinagar",
        "Boundaries: Rajasthan (north-east), Madhya Pradesh (east), Maharashtra (south-east and south), Pakistan (north-west — Kutch border), Arabian Sea (west)"
      ]
    },
    {
